    "title": "NBA Summer League debut dates revealed for AJ Dybantsa, Darryn Peterson and others - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Alex Walsh ,\n47 minutes ago\nThe NBA Draft is over, and fans won't have to wait long to see their favorite 2026 draft picks play in their first NBA games.\nThe 2026 NBA Summer League kicks off in just a few weeks, and we already know when we can see the debuts of a few of the top picks.\nNBA Summer League debut dates revealed for AJ Dybantsa, Darryn Peterson and others After the draft, the dates/times of two games were released for the Summer League.\nWe won't know until we get closer to the game if the teams' new players will definitely play, but we can at least prepare for the good chance that they will.\nMORE: Hornets engaged in trade offers on LaMelo Ball with these 2 teams\nJazz vs. Wizards on July 9 could feature the No. 1 pick, AJ Dybantsa, and the No. 2 pick, Darryn Peterson.\nThe following day is Bulls vs. Grizzlies , when we could see Cameron Boozer make his Memphis debut, and Caleb Wilson make his debut with the Bulls.\nOther games will be announced eventually, but the broadcast tonight highlighted these as two must-watch games to look forward to in a couple of weeks.\nMore NBA articles:",
    "summary": "The 2026 NBA Summer League kicks off in just a few weeks, and we already know when we can see the debuts of a few of the top picks. NBA Summer League debut dates revealed for AJ Dybantsa, Darryn Peterson and others After the draft, the dates/times of two games were released for the Summer League. We won't know until we get closer to the game if the teams' new players will definitely play, but we can at least prepare for the good chance that they will.",
